                        "entry_id": "e5bcbeb3-dd5f-3b56-ad39-d1aed526033f",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Any of various species of small parrot primarily of tropical regions."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "120bfd37-841b-45b4-b0b1-cb6d4e42d5eb",
                                "sense_id": "dc3dcfa9-447d-3b93-b2d9-5fa6fe3cef31",
                                "text": "we had loved them for our pastimes, as we do apes, monkies, or perokitoes, and not as man."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "f6a6e5bc-f9d6-464e-99bf-5e8255be57e0",
                                "sense_id": "dc3dcfa9-447d-3b93-b2d9-5fa6fe3cef31",
                                "text": "'Is it that it talks?' asked the lady. And the Phoenix replied in excellent French. It said, 'Parfaitement, madame!' 'Oh, the pretty parrakeet,' said the lady."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "3b8e3932-ef38-4a69-9736-1b4677c95954",
                                "sense_id": "dc3dcfa9-447d-3b93-b2d9-5fa6fe3cef31",
                                "text": "According to one legend, the parakeets escaped from the set of The African Queen, John Huston's 1951 film made at Shepperton studios."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
                "translations": [
                    {
                        "translation_id": "c6035f7f-635d-4272-95f5-6654efbbd944",
